# @glue — the morphism family-root substrate-decl. The Mesland
# correspondence as substrate primitive. A prism that does NOTHING
# but translate between two other prisms (spectral triples).
#
# Uses @fate for the translation decision; carries the typed
# restriction surface that defines which translations are admissible.
# The substrate-decl form of the morphism category that has been
# operating across @spectral/metalogue/tomm, @cascade, and the
# scattered code-translation species without yet being named at
# family-root altitude.
#
# === The recognition (#104 chain P5, 2026-06-30) ===
#
# This shard is the FIFTH tier of the #104 chain that began at
# @bauchladen (P1, `66e1ab8`) and advanced through @autopoietic
# (P2, `78edaa6`) and @fate (P3, `fdcba31`). P4 was the optical-
# keywords work (in flight). This tier lifts the morphism-category
# structure — already operating implicitly across multiple altitudes
# in the substrate — to family-root altitude as substrate-decl.
#
# The structural fact resolved earlier today: @glue is genuinely
# ABOVE @spectral/metalogue/tomm. Tomm probes are ONE species of
# @glue (the spectral-metalogue-altitude species). @cascade
# morphisms are ANOTHER species of @glue (the code-translation-
# altitude species). The yesterday's P4 `@cascade/code/formal/prose`
# (`437d061`) is YET ANOTHER species at the formal/prose altitude.
# @glue is the family-root containing these as siblings.
#
# Witnesses for the chain's #104 candidacy at this tier:
#   - Canonical spec at `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md`
#     §4.5 (the @glue × @fate composition pattern this shard
#     discharges); the five-step pattern (candidates → @fate algebra
#     → dice roll → apply → tray crystal) IS the @glue.translate
#     action's structural shape.
#   - `docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` `16f4564` §3 + §4 (Tomm
#     probes as Mesland-category morphisms; @cascade species as
#     Mesland-category objects; both substrate-decl'd at
#     `shards/spectral/metalogue.mirror` and `shards/cascade.mirror`
#     respectively); both already operate; @glue names the family
#     root they BOTH sit under as species.
#   - `shards/fate.mirror` at `fdcba31` (the dependency just landed;
#     @glue's forward-promise from the @fate shard at line 772-774
#     of `fate.mirror`: "@glue uses @fate to pick which morphism
#     to apply; @glue's selection IS a dice_roll; @glue discharges
#     fate_witnessing"; this shard discharges that forward promise).
#   - `shards/cascade.mirror` (the existing cross-language morphism
#     family-root; its `compile` / `measure` / `cascade` actions
#     ARE @glue.translate at the code-cascade altitude; this shard
#     lifts the discipline to the species-spanning altitude).
#   - The mathematical ancestors: Mesland 2013 (arXiv:1304.3802)
#     names the category of spectral triples with unbounded
#     KK-cycles as morphisms; Bertozzini-Conti-Lewkeeratiyutkul
#     2006 (*Osaka J. Math.* 43) provides the category-theoretic
#     formalization; Kasparov 1981 (*Math. USSR-Izv.* 16(3):513-572)
#     grounds the underlying KK-theory.
#
# === The "above @spectral/metalogue/tomm" resolution ===
#
# Earlier today's structural recognition (informally surfaced via
# substrate-pull cascade): the Tomm probes declared at
# `shards/spectral/metalogue.mirror` (recognition #100) are NOT the
# family-root of the morphism discipline. They are one ALTITUDE-
# SPECIFIC species of a more general substrate primitive — the
# Mesland correspondence between spectral triples.
#
# The three known species of @glue, with their altitudes and
# canonical declaration sites:
#
#   Species                         Altitude                  Declared at
#   -----------------------------   -----------------------   -------------
#   @spectral/metalogue/tomm        spectral-metalogue        shards/spectral/
#                                   (Bateson level V)         metalogue.mirror
#                                                              + tomm.mirror
#                                                              (recognition #100)
#   @cascade/code/<src>/<tgt>       code-translation          shards/cascade.mirror
#                                   (Bateson level IV)        + per-cascade species
#                                                              (recognition #95)
#   @cascade/code/formal/prose      formal/prose              `437d061` (yesterday's
#                                   (mid-altitude code         P4 landing)
#                                   ↔ NL morphism)
#
# These species WERE operating before this shard landed; the
# substrate ALREADY had the morphism machinery scattered across
# three sites. This shard's contribution is the family-root
# admission that absorbs them as siblings under one substrate-decl
# vocabulary. 54th-or-so instance of [[feedback-substrate-already-
# had-the-word]] at family-root altitude.
#
# The substrate-decl form of the absorption:
#
#   @glue                                        family-root (this shard)
#     ├── @spectral/metalogue/tomm               spectral-altitude species
#     ├── @cascade/code/<src>/<tgt>              cross-language species
#     └── @cascade/code/formal/prose             formal↔prose species
#
# Future @glue species (forward-promised, not landing this tick):
#   - @glue/kintsugi/<source>/<target>           transformation morphisms
#   - @glue/reflection/<source-altitude>/<target-altitude>
#                                                Reflection's altitude
#                                                selection as @glue
#   - @glue/pack/<from-agent>/<to-agent>         Pack-handoff morphisms
#                                                (per recognition #103)
#
# === Uses @fate for translation decisions: the composition mechanism ===
#
# @glue does NOT compute the translation directly. Per the canonical
# spec §4.5 (Reed memory entry confirms): @glue CARRIES the typed
# surface; @fate PICKS the morphism. The composition is:
#
#   @glue × @fate → typed translation outcome
#
# The structural form of the @glue.translate action below realizes
# this composition. Given a correspondence (the typed morphism
# surface) and a payload (the substrate state to translate), the
# action consults @fate to select WHICH morphism to apply within
# the correspondence's restriction surface. @fate's dice roll is
# bounded by the correspondence's (source_prism, target_prism,
# morphism_kind, restriction) tuple; the roll cannot land outside
# the typed restriction.
#
# This is what distinguishes @glue from a direct deterministic
# compute: the translation is STRUCTURALLY UNDERDETERMINED at the
# @glue altitude — there may be multiple admissible morphisms
# between the same (source, target) pair; @fate picks one within
# the restriction. The structural underdetermination IS what makes
# the morphism discipline a category rather than a function —
# Mesland's category has many morphisms between the same pair of
# objects; @glue inherits this.
#
# === The self-recursive use case forward-promise: @io/algebra ===
#
# Forward-promised composition: @glue × @kintsugi × @fate → @io/algebra
# (fold_back at P8). At a future tick in the #104 chain, the
# @kintsugi loop's per-step decisions will compose with @glue's
# translation discipline + @fate's selection to ground the @io/
# algebra surface — the substrate-decl form of how the substrate's
# output algebra COMPOSES across the @io boundary.
#
# Mechanism: the kintsugi loop emits candidate morphisms at each
# step (per `shards/fate.mirror` §4.6); each candidate morphism IS
# a @glue correspondence; @fate selects one; @glue applies it;
# the application's output crosses the @io boundary as a crystal
# in the appropriate @io/algebra/* sub-namespace.
#
# This forward-promise is structural: the @io/algebra discipline
# is NOT a new prism; it is the COMPOSITION of three existing
# prims (@glue, @kintsugi, @fate) at the boundary altitude. The
# composition lands at P8 of the chain; the family-root admission
# of @glue at this tick (P5) makes the composition addressable
# from the consumer side.
#
# === Inherits via `in @autopoietic` and `in @fate` ===
#
# @glue imports `in @fate` because @glue's translation decisions
# ARE @fate dice rolls; the inheritance is structural, not
# stylistic. Each @glue.translate emits a dice_roll (per
# `shards/fate.mirror`'s carrier); the dice_roll satisfies
# fate_witnessing per the inherited predicate; the translation
# outcome is a content-addressed crystal in the @bauchladen tray
# under `@fate/algebra/morphism` per spec §5.
#
# @glue imports `in @autopoietic` because @glue's morphism
# selections accumulate; future @glue.translate invocations consult
# prior morphism crystals via the tray; the read-write cycle on
# the tray IS Maturana-Varela's operational closure at the
# morphism-selection altitude. @glue is `in @autopoietic` is
# `in @bauchladen` (transitive); the chain's full discipline
# inheritance per spec §3.5 (forward-promised inheritors).
#
# @glue inherits the obligations @fate carries (autopoietic_
# membership_held + bauchladen_membership_held + dice_roll_
# constrained + bilateral_well_typed + optical_inference_grounded)
# via the inheritance chain. The bilateral commitment (per
# recognition #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`):
# @glue's body discharges all five obligations at the realisation
# boundary; consumers surface violations at the species boundary.
#
# === The categorical composition: non-commutative per [ω, ω] cross-term ===
#
# Per the curvature-and-tomm reference (`docs/math/the-tower/
# curvature-and-tomm.md` §5): the curvature 2-form Ω = dω + ½[ω, ω]
# carries a non-trivial cross-term [ω, ω] that lives where altitude
# transitions happen. The @glue.compose action below inherits this:
# categorical composition of correspondences is NON-COMMUTATIVE in
# general, because the cross-altitude composition c2 ∘ c1 carries
# the curvature cross-term that c1 ∘ c2 does not.
#
# This is the structural reason @glue.compose returns a
# correspondence rather than a verdict: the composed correspondence
# is itself a typed morphism with its own restriction surface,
# whose discharge may require additional @fate consultation. The
# Mesland category's composition is the Kasparov intersection
# product (per Mesland 2013 §3); the substrate-altitude form is
# what @glue.compose declares.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@glue/*` species sub-shard
# or operational Rust sibling lands at this tick. The substrate
# ALREADY has operational machinery at the species altitudes
# (@spectral/metalogue/tomm at the spectral altitude, @cascade
# species at the code-translation altitude, `437d061` at the
# formal/prose altitude). This shard names the family-root
# substrate-decl contract so downstream species can declare `in
# @glue` and `requires glue_witnessing(my_correspondence)` rather
# than re-state the morphism-category obligation per species.
